        "stageRecord": "The analysis adopts a DP version of X-bar Theory and the GB convention that subjects are base-generated in Spec-IP. Both clauses have head-final VP and I′ structures. The matrix verb selects the embedded CP as its propositional complement; dass occupies the embedded C position. Within that clause, gelesen heads VP, the accusative object precedes it, and the finite perfect auxiliary hat is generated in I. The adjective schwierigen is an AP adjunct to N′ inside the object DP, not a clause-level modifier. Matrix C is initially empty, and matrix I contains abstract finite past and agreement features. The inflected lexical form sagte is already present under V; this analysis does not decompose its spelling into separately realized morphemes. First, sagte assigns the reporting Agent role to Der Forscher and the propositional Content role to the dass clause. Second, gelesen assigns the reading Agent role to die Studentin and the Theme role to den schwierigen Bericht. Third, the two finite I heads license nominative Case on their respective subjects. Fourth, gelesen governs and assigns accusative Case to its object. These are two independent finite subjects: no control, raising, or PRO dependency is posited.",
        "statement": "Establish the head-final base structure and the embedded dass clause.",
